{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>My God</b> — Because he mentioned Elohim without the sign of the speaker, he mentioned Elohai, which is the sign of the speaker, to single it out. Therefore he said: Elohai." "<b>Let them be made like galgal</b> — The gimel is added because it is like when dung (gelal) is swept away, and like galgal before the whirlwind, for it rolls (mitgallel)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 83, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:55.809855257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}